content.text:
Payment is the single root cause. Its pod stopped serving spans at about 03:25 and its CPU stayed at zero, which is what checkout's failing `Charge` calls and the frontend 500s trace back to.

```json
{
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "service": "payment",
      "fault_kind": "pod_unavailable",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, attr_span_kind, attr_status_code, COUNT(*) n, approx_quantile(duration/1e6,0.95) p95_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='checkout' AND span_name='oteldemo.PaymentService/Charge' GROUP BY ALL",
          "claim": "Checkout's PaymentService/Charge client calls all error in about 0.18 ms (46 spans); payment emits no spans in the abnormal window."
        },
        {
          "kind": "metric",
          "sql": "SELECT DATE_TRUNC('minute', time) m, metric, ROUND(AVG(value),1) v FROM abnormal_metrics WHERE service_name='payment' AND metric IN ('k8s.pod.cpu.usage','k8s.pod.memory.usage') GROUP BY ALL ORDER BY metric, m",
          "claim": "Payment pod memory falls from about 111 MB to about 3 MB and CPU drops to zero from 03:25 onward."
        },
        {
          "kind": "metric",
          "sql": "SELECT 'abn' p, metric, attr_k8s_pod_name pod, MIN(time) t0, MAX(time) t1, MIN(value) mn, MAX(value) mx, COUNT(*) n FROM abnormal_metrics WHERE attr_k8s_pod_name LIKE 'payment%' AND metric = 'k8s.container.restarts' GROUP BY ALL",
          "claim": "Payment container restart counter moves from 0 to 1 during the abnormal window, versus 0 throughout normal."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "propagation": [
    {
      "from": "payment",
      "to": "checkout",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, attr_span_kind, attr_status_code, COUNT(*) n FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='checkout' AND attr_status_code='Error' GROUP BY ALL",
          "claim": "Checkout's Charge client spans and PlaceOrder server spans both go to Error status once payment is down."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "from": "checkout",
      "to": "frontend",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, attr_span_kind, attr_status_code, attr_http_response_status_code, COUNT(*) n FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='frontend' AND attr_status_code='Error' GROUP BY ALL",
          "claim": "Frontend calls to checkout fail with HTTP 500 status, producing 500s on frontend server spans (214 in the abnormal window)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "from": "frontend",
      "to": "frontend-proxy",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, attr_span_kind, attr_status_code, attr_http_response_status_code, COUNT(*) n FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='frontend-proxy' AND attr_status_code='Error' GROUP BY ALL",
          "claim": "Frontend-proxy server spans return HTTP 500 (116) and its client calls to frontend fail with 500, reaching the user-facing entry point."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

